[center][size=6][b]SkyParkour Together[/b][/size]
[size=4]Parkour Animations Sync for Skyrim Together Reborn[/size][/center]

Your friends see your parkour. When you vault a fence, climb a wall, grab a ledge, step up, slide or land in a roll with [b]SkyParkour[/b], everyone in your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] session sees the same animation on your character, at the same height and variant you got. No more watching a friend float up a cliff in a running pose.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Every SkyParkour move is shared[/b]: vaults, climbs, low and high ledge grabs, steps (including weapon-out steps that play on the legs only), slides and landing rolls, at your playback speed setting.
[*][b]The same animation on every screen[/b]: the graph values SkyParkour uses to pick an animation go along with each move, so other players see the exact animation you played.
[*][b]Works with the official Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.4[/b] from Nexus, on Skyrim [b]1.7.104[/b] and [b]1.6.1170 / 1.6.1179[/b].
[*][b]No server changes[/b]: it plays on any regular server of your Skyrim Together version.
[*][b]SkyParkour itself is untouched[/b]: this mod contains no SkyParkour files and changes nothing about how parkour plays for you.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Every player in the session[/b] needs all of these:
[list]
[*]Skyrim Special/Anniversary Edition [b]1.6.1170, 1.6.1179 or 1.7.104[/b]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] for your game version
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url] [b]1.8.4[/b]
[*][b]SkyParkour[/b] by Tsptds, from its own Nexus page (not included)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Which Skyrim Together do I have?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.8.4 (official)[/b]: Skyrim Together Reborn from its Nexus page, for Skyrim 1.7.104 or 1.6.1170/1.6.1179.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Skyrim Together only starts when its launcher sits in the same folder as the rest of Skyrim Together ([font=Courier New]libcef.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]EarlyLoad.dll[/font], the UI...). How you get this mod's launcher there depends on your mod manager.
[list=1]
[*]Install Skyrim Together Reborn and SkyParkour as usual.
[*]Install this mod. The installer asks which Skyrim Together you use, then your game version.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Mod Organizer 2[/b][/size]
MO2 starts a launcher from its real folder on disk, so mod order is not enough. Copy the launcher once:
[list=1]
[*]Right-click [b]SkyParkour Together[/b] > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]Right-click your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] mod > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]In the Skyrim Together folder, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] to [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] (your backup).
[*]Copy [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the SkyParkour Together folder into the Skyrim Together folder.
[*]Keep SkyParkour Together enabled (it provides the SKSE plugin) and start the game with your usual MO2 entry for Skyrim Together, the one pointing into the Skyrim Together Reborn mod. [b]Don't[/b] point an MO2 entry at the SkyParkour Together folder: the launcher can't start from there and simply closes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Vortex[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Set SkyParkour Together to load [b]after[/b] Skyrim Together Reborn and deploy.
[*]Start the game from [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] as you normally start Skyrim Together.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Is it working?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/SkyParkourTogether.log[/font] says [i]"Skyrim Together add-on found"[/i].
[*]Skyrim Together's log ([font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/logs[/font]) contains [i]"mod sync: SkyParkour Together 1.0.1 ... registered"[/i].
[/list]
[b]The launcher closes straight away[/b] (no window, no log): it was started from a folder without the rest of Skyrim Together. In MO2, do the copy steps above.
[b]The SKSE log says the add-on was not found:[/b] the game started with a different [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font]. In MO2, check the copied launcher is the one in the Skyrim Together Reborn mod; in Vortex, check the load order.

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]
SkyParkour plays its animations directly on your character's animation graph, which Skyrim Together does not share, so other players only saw you slide around in a running pose. This mod has two parts:
[list]
[*][b]SkyParkourTogether.dll[/b] (SKSE plugin): tells Skyrim Together which of your animations are SkyParkour's and which values pick the right one. It reads no game memory, so one DLL works on every game version.
[*][b]SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] for your Skyrim Together and game version: that exact Skyrim Together release with a small add-on, the [i]STR Mod Sync API[/i], that sends those animations through Skyrim Together's existing animation relay and plays them on your character on the other players' screens. It is the same launcher our other mods ship (it also carries RaceMenu Together's add-on, which stays off unless that mod is installed), so they never fight over it. Nothing else in Skyrim Together is changed.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]RaceMenu Together[/b]: fully compatible. Both mods ship the identical launcher carrying both add-ons, so install them in any order and both work. Keep both up to date.
[*][b]Other mods that replace or patch SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] (other Skyrim Together forks, STRPluginMessagingAPI) conflict with this mod: only one launcher can be used.
[*]Works alongside other SkyParkour add-ons and animation mods.
[*]Mods that add their own parkour animation events outside SkyParkour's names are not shared.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
[b]MO2:[/b] delete the copied [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the Skyrim Together Reborn mod, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] back, then remove this mod. [b]Vortex:[/b] remove the mod.

